  "body": "Today the in-app chat model gets the MCP tool list but not the guidance that the camcraft-mcp skill (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/`) gives Claude Code: the job workflow (stock, tools, operations, generate, verify, post), which parameters matter, and common refusals. Requests such as \"add a facing operation after this 2D Adaptive\" depend on it.\n\nWanted: a condensed skill text, generated from or tested against the camcraft-mcp skill so the two do not drift, sent as the chat's system instructions. A size cap (it rides on every request and costs tokens), a test that fails when it exceeds the cap or names a tool the registry does not have. A short note in the panel that the assistant has the CamCraft guide.\n\nDone means: with a cloud provider, the request above produces a Face operation after the 2D Adaptive through undoable commands. The size and drift tests pass.\n\nUser validation (reporter, 2026-11-23): before this merges, the reporter (mkinney) hand-tests a build of the PR in the desktop app and confirms it is usable. The PR stays a draft until that confirmation is on the PR.\n",
